<title>UK: Unichem plans to run doctors services - Report.</title>
<headline>Unichem plans to run doctors services - Report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Drugs wholesaler and retailer UniChem Plc is planning to bid for family doctor services for Britain's National Health Service (NHS), the Financial Times said on Monday.</p>
<p>The report said legal changes planned for next year would make it easier for private bodies to employ staff to provide services for the NHS.</p>
<p>It said UniChem wanted to set up one-stop health shops combining doctors' services, minor surgery, chiropody, dental care and a pharmacy.</p>
<p>The report said supermarket chains Tesco Plc and ASDA Group Plc are understood to be exploring similar schemes for their stores.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
